Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 09:26:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 126/154] feat(peek): the card keeps a placeholder while its
 page loads
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

An adopted popup dropped the loading placeholder the moment it was
adopted, and since the off-site link change every target=_blank link
takes that path, so the card was a see-through window over the dimmed
page until the page painted. The placeholder now stays until the first
paint, in the overlay paper with a throbber, and drops at once only
for a blank popup or a navigation that never commits. The origin chip
names the target host from the start and wears the overlay surface,
ink, chip radius and hairline, with the danger ink for Not secure.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 chrome/browser/ui/browser.cc | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/browser.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/browser.cc
index 4c47c74c49f96..29df7e61e460b 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/browser.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/browser.cc
@@ -1753,7 +1753,8 @@ content::WebContents* Browser::AddNewContents(
     content::WebContents* peeked = new_contents.get();
     // A refused adopt hands the popup back, and it falls through to the stock
     // path below still owned - never destroyed under the caller.
-    new_contents = atrium::AdoptPopupAsPeek(this, std::move(new_contents));
+    new_contents =
+        atrium::AdoptPopupAsPeek(this, std::move(new_contents), target_url);
     if (!new_contents) {
       return peeked;
     }
